\section{Finding Recursive Calls That Consume Nothing}

A combinator library can detect one source of nontermination before
generating recursive parser functions. Work on a finite grammar
represented by named rules and expressions for epsilon, tokens,
choice, sequence, and rule calls. Assume pure combinators with
unordered alternatives and no dynamic bind or lookahead predicates.
First compute the least fixed point of nullability. Next build a
graph whose edge $A\to B$ means the body of $A$ can reach a call of
$B$ before consuming any input. Traverse each sequence until the
first nonnullable child, and visit every branch of a choice. The
output is a cycle witness or a certificate that this particular
zero-consumption graph is acyclic.

\begin{sudocode}
  \Input rule bodies $R$ and their fixed-point nullability
  \Output a cycle witness or an acyclic graph
  \Function{Leading}{$e$}
    \If{$e$ is a call to $B$}
      \State \Return $\{B\}$ \Comment{Record, do not unfold}
    \ElsIf{$e$ is a sequence of children $C$}
      \State $L\gets\varnothing$
      \ForAll{$p$ in $C$ in source order}
        \State $L\gets L\cup\Call{Leading}{p}$
        \If{$p$ is not nullable} \Comment{Later calls must advance}
          \State \Return $L$
        \EndIf
      \EndFor
      \State \Return $L$
    \ElsIf{$e$ is a choice of children $C$}
      \State \Return $\bigcup_{p\in C}\Call{Leading}{p}$
    \EndIf
    \State \Return $\varnothing$
  \EndFunction
  \State $G\gets\{(A,B): B\in\Call{Leading}{R[A]}\}$
  \State \Return a cycle in $G$ if one exists, else $G$
\end{sudocode}

Use $A\to H B\mid y$, $H\to\epsilon\mid z$, and $B\to A x\mid w$.
Nullability marks $H$ but neither $A$ nor $B$. The graph has edges
$A\to H$, $A\to B$, and $B\to A$. In particular, the call to $B$
is reachable through the empty alternative of $H$; the final
token $x$ cannot guard the earlier call to $A$. Cycle detection
returns $A,B,A$. If the first production instead starts with
$z B$, the only remaining edge is $B\to A$. This graph accepts
the revision, without ruling on one-token predictability.

For each edge, the skipped sequence prefix has an epsilon derivation.
Conversely, any direct recursive call reached without consumption
is encountered by this traversal. Keep source sites on the edges
so a cycle report can show the rule call and the nullable prefix
responsible. A strongly connected component pass is linear in the
graph size; singleton components are cyclic only if they have a
self edge. Passing this check does not establish that a separate
repetition combinator has a consuming body, so check repetition
progress independently if the library provides it.
